# Telemetry (opt-in)

PsyClaw is local-first. Sentry and PostHog stay off unless you set the matching
environment variables. Unset keys mean: no SDK import, no init, no outbound
telemetry.

Copy this file to `.env` in your shell environment (do not commit `.env`).

# Node / CLI agent — Sentry project slug: psyclaw
SENTRY_DSN=

# Browser panel + website — Sentry project slug: psyclaw-web
SENTRY_DSN_WEB=
# Optional alias for static / hosted web builds:
# PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# PostHog project API key (phc_…). Used by the Node CLI.
POSTHOG_KEY=
# Browser panel/website. Falls back to POSTHOG_KEY when unset.
PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to https://us.posthog.com
POSTHOG_HOST=
# PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=

# Optional. Defaults to psyclaw@<package.json version>
# SENTRY_RELEASE=
# SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=
